  {
   "key": "scene_02",
   "text": "France arrive having won 3 of their last 5, but they lost the latest, 3-1 away in Italy. Turkiye have lost all 5. Yalçın promised a change. His words, in translation: tomorrow we will play a bit more in control. Türkiye Today adds that he meant a more defensive position, still with one striker. And he had fewer players to choose from. Ozan Kabak and Ümit Akdağ were both suspended. So the yardstick is clear: France to attack, Turkiye to sit deep and wait.",
