  {
   "key": "scene_07",
   "text": "Now the part the scoreline hides. FotMob's data places every shot on the pitch, sized by xG. Look at how many of France's are close to goal. France's xG is 3.36. Turkiye's is 1.54. That points to a France win by far more than one goal, and it says Yalçın's deeper block did not stop the chances. What kept Turkiye alive was their goalkeeper. Berke Özer made 7 saves. He kept the plan breathing. So when minute 90 came, one corner was enough, and the header that scored was Turkiye's best chance of the night, by FotMob's numbers.",
